WEBVTT

00:01:58.232 --> 00:02:01.222
you wouldn't be in this situation at this moment

00:02:01.222 --> 00:02:02.999
with some doctor you've never met

00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:06.814
about to amputate your foot.

00:02:06.814 --> 00:02:10.456
Why did I feel justified in judging her?

00:02:10.456 --> 00:02:13.025
I'd like to say I don't know.

00:02:13.025 --> 00:02:15.061
But I actually do.

00:02:15.061 --> 00:02:17.392
You see, in the hubris of my youth,

00:02:17.392 --> 00:02:20.496
I thought I had her all figured out.

00:02:20.496 --> 00:02:22.326
She ate too much. She got unlucky.

00:02:22.326 --> 00:02:25.695
She got diabetes. Case closed.

00:02:25.695 --> 00:02:27.098
Ironically, at that time in my life,

00:02:27.098 --> 00:02:29.496
I was also doing cancer research,

00:02:29.496 --> 00:02:31.839
immune-based therapies for melanoma, to be specific,